  {
    "parts": [
      {
        "content": "## Summary\n\n**Target Fact:** `F:ml430-int-add-modeq-left-ee732b5b` - `Int.add_modEq_left`\n\n**Formal Statement:** `∀ {n a : ℤ}, n + a ≡ a [ZMOD n]`\n\n**Structural Shape:** This is a modular equivalence fact stating that adding the modulus `n` to any integer `a` yields a value congruent to `a` modulo `n`. It's a foundational property of modular arithmetic with no dependencies and unlocks nothing.\n\n**Available Premises:** The Int prelude contains 20 modEq theorems including:\n- `Int.modEq_refl`, `Int.modEq_symm`, `Int.modEq_trans` (equivalence relation properties)\n- `Int.modEq_add_left`, `Int.modEq_add_right` (congruence preservation under addition with hypothesis)\n- `Int.modEq_iff_dvd` (characterization via divisibility)\n- `Int.add_comm`, `Int.add_assoc`, `Int.add_zero` (addition properties)\n\n**Similar Eligible Facts:** The frontier contains structurally identical facts:\n1. `F:ml430-int-add-modeq-right-e58108ee` - `∀ {n a : ℤ}, a + n ≡ a [ZMOD n]` (commuted version)\n2. `F:ml430-nat-add-modeq-left-e3b1fba9` - `∀ {n a : ℕ}, n + a ≡ a [MOD n]` (natural number version)\n3. `F:ml430-nat-add-modeq-right-e2f11f21` - `∀ {n a : ℕ}, a + n ≡ a [MOD n]` (natural number commuted)\n\n**Registry Status:** No operations currently target this fact (0 registered operations for it).",
        "id": null,
        "provider_name": null,
        "provider_details": null,
        "part_kind": "text"
      }
    ],
